---
// DRAFT copy — a coached first pass on Kha's career story. Keep editing
// until every sentence sounds like something he'd actually say out loud.
const STORY = [
  "I graduated in Mechatronics Engineering from Ho Chi Minh City University of Technology, then joined Keppel Land Vietnam's Management Associate program — a rotation built for future business leaders, not for data people.",
  "That's where the spark started, though I didn't notice it at the time. Coordinating an 816-unit handover, I built Excel trackers just to make sense of what was happening — which contractors were behind, which units still had defects, what the team needed to look at that week. I wasn't chasing data as a career. I just liked that a formula could tell me the truth faster than a meeting could.",
  "That spark followed me to KONE and grew there — from reading a spreadsheet to building the dashboards an entire operations team relied on, then teaching myself SQL and Python simply because I wanted to understand more, before I even had a problem that needed them.",
  "The same curiosity brought me to Prudential, where I now build the systems a life insurer's agency network trusts for real decisions — and it's what's pulling me toward the next layer, Analytics Engineering, the pipelines underneath the dashboards. I don't think it burns out. I think it's what keeps taking me further.",
];
---

<section class="section" id="about">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <h2 data-reveal>About</h2>
    <div class="about-story">
      {STORY.map((paragraph) => <p data-reveal>{paragraph}</p>)}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .about-story {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  .about-story p {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
  }
</style>
